<task id="030" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>New `@spaarke/communication-components` lib + rich Pattern D workspace widget (copy `CalendarWorkspaceWidget`); upgrade `communications-list` IN PLACE (keep type string + section id); dual-deploy LegalWorkspace + SpaarkeAi</title>
    <phase>W3 — Workspace Widget Upgrade (Surface 3) — upgrade-in-place</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>14</estimated-hours>
    <deps>010</deps>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, spaarke-ai</tags>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Creates a NEW load-bearing shared library (`@spaarke/communication-components`) + a rich Pattern D workspace widget (`.tsx`/`.ts`) that replaces the thin `communications-list` surface used by BOTH LegalWorkspace and SpaarkeAi; architecture-level decisions (new-lib boundary per §11, Pattern D dual-use shape, filter-chip toolbar + card strip + embedded `<DataGrid hostFilters onRecordOpen>` + row-click modal, keep-type-string dispatch invariant); dual-deploy is the R1/prior trap (NFR-07); merge-order coordination with `spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2` + open PR #508. ADR-021 (Fluent v9), ADR-012 (shared lib) bind; ADR-021 dark-mode is a hard UI-test gate. FULL is non-negotiable.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W3</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>All-client TypeScript in a NEW `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/**` package plus two narrow edits (`register-workspace-widgets.ts`, `communications.registration.ts`); disjoint by file + language from the concurrent BFF (C#) tracks and the schema/PCF tracks. Coordinate MERGE ORDER (not concurrency) with `spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2` (`@spaarke/legal-workspace` extraction + section-registry) and open PR #508 (Events.Components package boundary that this task copies from) — see &lt;notes&gt;.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-12</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Upgrade the existing thin `communications-list` workspace widget to a **rich Calendar-style Pattern D widget** (FR-12). Today the widget is a bare `<DataGrid>` mounted via `DataverseEntityViewWidget` (no cards, no filter chips, no chrome). Make it a first-class dual-use widget with a filter-chip toolbar + a card strip + an embedded `<DataGrid hostFilters onRecordOpen>` + a row-click modal — copying the shape of `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Events.Components/src/widgets/CalendarWorkspaceWidget/CalendarWorkspaceWidget.tsx`.

    The rich widget content lives in a **NEW shared library `@spaarke/communication-components`** at `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/`. §11: the Events lib is entity-coupled (calendar/event semantics) and `@spaarke/ai-widgets` is a thin-generic layer — neither is the right home for rich communication widget content (investigation §4). Do NOT bloat ai-widgets or couple into the Events lib; the new lib is the cohesive home.

    **Upgrade `communications-list` IN PLACE — do NOT add a second widget (NFR-05).** You MUST:
    - **Keep the type string `communications-list`** in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/widgets/workspace/register-workspace-widgets.ts` (the Direct/dual-use registration, ~line 733). Renaming it breaks AI-router + section dispatch.
    - **Keep the section id `communications`** (and the `communications-list` widgetType) in `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/sections/communications.registration.ts`. Point its `renderContent` at the new rich widget instead of the bare `DataverseEntityViewWidget`, preserving `configId` = `e1826c4c-9575-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4a05` (the shipped "Active Communications" grid config — reuse, no second default).
    - Register the new rich widget component through the same `registerWorkspaceWidget('communications-list', …)` call — one registration, upgraded factory, same contract `WorkspaceWidgetComponent<TData>` (`Spaarke.AI.Widgets/src/types/widget-types.ts`).

    Row-click opens Layout 1 (OOB modal via `Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo` at 85% × 85%) through the DataGrid framework's `defaultRecordOpen`/`onRecordOpen` — mirror the existing behavior; do NOT re-implement modal mechanics. Advanced filter state pipes through the `<DataGrid hostFilters={…}/>` prop (`fetchXmlOverlay.ts`), exactly as `CalendarWorkspaceWidget` pipes its filter row.

    **DUAL-DEPLOY (NFR-07)**: widget/shared-lib changes MUST rebuild BOTH `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/` and `src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/`. This is the R1/prior dual-deploy trap — a change deployed to only one surface renders stale in the other.

    Fluent UI v9 only (ADR-021): `@fluentui/react-components` + `makeStyles` + `tokens`; dark mode passes through the host `FluentProvider`; no hardcoded colors. No BFF changes — the widget reads via `Xrm.WebApi` through `XrmDataverseClient` (investigation §4).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React 18/19 + TypeScript developer fluent in Fluent UI v9 (`makeStyles`/`tokens`/`FluentProvider`), the SpaarkeAi workspace-widget model (`WorkspaceWidgetComponent`, `registerWorkspaceWidget`, Pattern D dual-use), the Spaarke DataGrid framework (`<DataGrid configId hostFilters onRecordOpen>`, chip auto-derivation, `fetchXmlOverlay`), and the dual-deploy discipline for shared-lib widget changes. Familiar with `CalendarWorkspaceWidget` as the canonical Pattern D reference.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new `@spaarke/communication-components` shared library exists at `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/` exporting a rich Pattern D communications widget (filter-chip toolbar + card strip + embedded `<DataGrid configId="e1826c4c-9575-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4a05" hostFilters onRecordOpen>` + row-click modal), copied in shape from `CalendarWorkspaceWidget.tsx`. The existing `communications-list` Direct registration (`register-workspace-widgets.ts`) and the `communications` section registration (`communications.registration.ts`) are upgraded IN PLACE to mount it — the type string `communications-list` and section id `communications` are UNCHANGED (dispatch unbroken). Exactly ONE widget registration (no second widget). The change is dual-deployed to LegalWorkspace + SpaarkeAi. Builds + lint clean; dark-mode + semantic-token compliant (ADR-021); the widget renders in both hosts.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Surface 3 of R2 upgrades the workspace widget from thin to rich. The thin `communications-list` widget already exists in both wrappers: the Direct registration (`register-workspace-widgets.ts` ~line 733) and the section shim (`communications.registration.ts`), plus `sectionRegistry.ts` line 120 + `scripts/system-layouts.json` (sortOrder 6). Today it renders a bare `<DataGrid>` via `DataverseEntityViewWidget` — no cards, no filter chips, no chrome (investigation §4). R2 makes it a first-class Pattern D dual-use widget matching the shipped Calendar widget's richness.

      §11 Component Justification (concrete cost-of-doing-nothing): the NEW `@spaarke/communication-components` lib is justified because there is no cohesive home for rich communication widget content — the Events lib (`@spaarke/events-components`) is entity-coupled (calendar/event semantics) and `@spaarke/ai-widgets` is a thin-generic layer (investigation §4). Existing overlap (grep-verified): none that hosts rich comm content. Extension test: neither the Events lib nor ai-widgets can host this without either coupling comm content into calendar semantics or bloating the generic layer. Cost-of-doing-nothing: rich widget content has no cohesive home and forces coupling into the Events lib or bloats ai-widgets. The WIDGET UPGRADE itself is extend-only (no §11 justification needed) — it extends the existing `communications-list` registration in place; the ONLY new component is the lib.

      NFR-05 (no duplication): MUST NOT add a second widget registration. Upgrade the existing `communications-list` in place; keep the type string + section id. The grid config `e1826c4c-9575-f111-ab0e-7ced8ddc4a05` is REUSED (single default) — do NOT create a colliding second `sprk_isdefault` config.

      NFR-07 (dual-deploy): the R1/prior trap. Any change to a shared lib the widget lives in, or to the widget registration, requires rebuilding BOTH LegalWorkspace and SpaarkeAi. A one-surface deploy leaves the other rendering the stale widget.

      Merge-order coordination (plan §3 hot-path): `spaarke-dataset-grid-framework-r2` is actively touching `@spaarke/legal-workspace` extraction + the section-registry, and open PR #508 changes the Events.Components package boundary that this task copies from. This is a MERGE-ORDER concern, not a concurrency one — run `/conflict-check` before the PR and coordinate landing order so the copied `CalendarWorkspaceWidget` shape and the section-registry edits do not diverge. See &lt;notes&gt;.

      Reference the Pattern D dual-use archetype: `docs/guides/BUILD-A-NEW-WORKSPACE-WIDGET.md` (Calendar canonical). No BFF changes — the widget reads via `Xrm.WebApi` through `XrmDataverseClient` (`docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md`); root §10 (BFF hygiene, publish-size, CVE) does NOT apply.
    </background>
